{"id": "EUVD-2026-50171", "enisaUuid": "c5ed6078-493c-32a8-bf83-575ac39a0143", "description": "Apache Traffic Server copies the client Host header into a fixed-size stack buffer without a bound during redirect handling, so an over-long Host header overflows the stack when redirect following is enabled.\n\n\n\nThis issue affects Apache Traffic Server: from 8.0.0 through 8.1.11, from 9.0.0 through 9.2.14, from 10.0.0 through 10.1.3.\n\n\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 9.2.15 or 10.1.4, which fix the issue.", "datePublished": "2026-07-29T07:23:54", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-01T16:57:26", "baseScore": 8.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://lists.apache.org/thread/5prl9glcm9g2swnq9hqxvnokylm1gr6d"], "aliases": ["GHSA-4p58-9v5g-254v", "CVE-2026-33930"], "assigner": "apache", "epss": 0.58, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "57dfbdf9-d858-34ed-9851-2a34586eb333", "product": {"name": "Apache Traffic Server", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}, "product_version": "9.0.0 \u22649.2.14"}, {"id": "86a75ab6-0604-3e71-ac33-37bc7f55c965", "product": {"name": "Apache Traffic Server", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}, "product_version": "8.0.0 \u22648.1.11"}, {"id": "bea50ca4-6d30-3c61-9400-d96b8a0d09fc", "product": {"name": "Apache Traffic Server", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}, "product_version": "10.0.0 \u226410.1.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1bd66a3c-d6c9-386f-8e98-36e19f6584f2", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}], "isExploited": false}